From 8dbad19c893c46d66bac3a4a4a56c90b74823531 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:35:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] The trading post: a board in Edgeville to sell, buy and
 barter on

A new loc, "Trading post", stands at 12,36 of m48_54 - beside ::home, facing east
across the road to the bank door. Browse, Sell and Collect; use an item on it to see
who is selling one. The market itself is the engine's (engine/market/TradingPost.ts
and the tp_* commands); this is the post, the windows and the script between them.

THE MODEL is not from the cache. tools/models/gentradingpostmodel.py in the root repo
builds it from OSRS parts - the frame of the Shooting Star noticeboard, a strongbox, a
crate, coins, a sack - scaled, placed and merged into one .ob2, because a loc config
has no per-model offset. The board's star chart and moon crest are cut out and
replaced: a tiled cork panel with seven pinned notices, and a gold medallion. Tiled
because the client sorts faces by their centres, and one board-sized triangle beat half
the notices from any three-quarter view.

THREE MAIN WINDOWS AND ONE SIDE (tools/gentradingpost.py, --check to verify):
tradingpost for the lists (Browse, My listings, My offers, Collection box),
tradingpost_listing for one listing and its offers, tradingpost_offer for building an
offer, and tradingpost_side for the inventory beside them. Three panels rather than
one with hidden layers because opening another panel is what fires [if_close] on the
barter window, and that is the one place its items can be handed back - on Back, Close,
walking off and logging out alike.

SELLER NAMES AND OFFERS ARE PUBLIC: anyone looking at a listing sees who is selling and
who has offered what, as a line of text. Only the seller can open an offer's items and
accept or decline it.

BUY NOW, ACCEPT AND TAKE DOWN want a second click on the same button; the first arms
%tp_confirm and the button says what the second will do. Every other click disarms it.

scripts/engine.rs2 declares the thirty tp_* commands and p_namedialog / last_string,
which the Search button uses. Login reads out what happened while the player was
away, via ~tp_login.

tools/tradingpost_battery.py (and in content.yml): the barter inv goes back whatever
closes it, every tp_ action's answer is kept and looked at, the three confirm clicks
arm before they act and nothing else calls what they guard, every button is wired,
and the loc, its ids, its model and the map line agree. Deleting the barter hand-back,
or the Buy now arm, each fails it.

Building locally needed the git-ignored server-only packs (dbrow, param, hunt, ...)
deleted and regenerated - they were older than their sources but newer on disk - and
BUILD_VERIFY=false for a .seq checksum mismatch that predates this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
